"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith=self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith||[]).push([[27754],{227754:e=>{e.exports='# Find a Security Case\n\nHow to find or retrieve a **security case** by ID (either uuid or short-ID like sec-1234), by title/description, or by listing security cases with **filters** and **sorting**. Use when the user asks to view, get, or open a specific security case, or to search security cases (e.g. open security cases, high severity, unassigned, newest first).\n\n## Common questions and filter/sort conditions\n\nUse **apiListLakewatchSecurityCases** (it lists SECURITY_CASE / security cases only). Pass `null` or empty for any filter you don\'t need.\n\n| User question / intent                              | Filters / sort to use                                                                                   |\n| --------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| “Show me open security cases”                       | `state: ["OPEN"]`, others empty array or null                                                           |\n| “List resolved security cases”                      | `state: ["RESOLVED"]`, others empty array or null                                                       |\n| “High severity security cases”                      | `severity: ["HIGH"]`, others empty array or null                                                        |\n| “Security cases that need attention” / “unassigned” | `unassigned: true`, `state: ["OPEN"]` or `[]`, others empty array or null                               |\n| “Security cases assigned to me”                     | `assigneeId: "<user id>"`, others null                                                                  |\n| “Security cases for rule X”                         | `ruleId: "<rule id>"`, others null                                                                      |\n| “Security cases with ‘login’ in the title”          | `titleSearch: "login"`, others null                                                                     |\n| “Security cases created before last week”           | `createdBefore: "<ISO timestamp>"`, others null                                                         |\n| “Newest security cases first”                       | `orderByColumn: "created_at"`, `orderByDirection: "desc"`, filters as needed                            |\n| “Recently updated security cases”                   | `orderByColumn: "last_modified_at"`, `orderByDirection: "desc"`, filters as needed                      |\n| “Open high-severity security cases”                 | `state: ["OPEN"]`, `severity: ["HIGH"]`, others empty array or null                                     |\n| “All security cases” (no filter)                    | `state: []`, `severity: []`, other filters null; use `orderByColumn`/`orderByDirection` if sort desired |\n\n**Filter values**: `state` and `severity` accept **multiple values** (arrays). `state` — OPEN, IN_PROGRESS, MITIGATED, RESOLVED, DUPLICATE, STATE_UNSPECIFIED. `severity` — INFORMATIONAL, MEDIUM, HIGH, CRITICAL, CASE_SEVERITY_UNSPECIFIED. Pass empty array to omit.\n\n## User provides a security case ID\n\nWhen the user gives a security case uuid ID or a short ID like sec-1234 directly, call `apiGetLakewatchResourceById` with `resourceType: "security-case"` and `resourceId` set to that ID.\n\n```json\n{\n  "thoughts": "User provided security case ID. Retrieving the security case directly.",\n  "resourceType": "security-case",\n  "resourceId": "case-id-here"\n}\n```\n\n## User provides a security case name or description\n\nWhen the user references a security case by title or filter value:\n\n1. Call **apiListLakewatchSecurityCases** with `thoughts`, `limit` (e.g. 100), and the filter/sort that matches the user\'s intent (see table above).\n2. Search the list for a security case matching the title; match case-insensitively and allow partial matches.\n3. Extract the security case ID from the response.\n4. Call **apiGetLakewatchResourceById** with `resourceType: "security-case"` and that `resourceId`.\n\n5. If the user\'s request is to search more generally (full search across description and comments) you can use the apiSearchLakewatchCases tool. This will return results with a bit of context around each match. You can then use apiGetLakewatchResourceById to get the whole case for each match that seems relevant.\n\n**Filtering**: `titleSearch`, `state` (array of values; empty to omit), `severity` (array of values; empty to omit), `unassigned`, `createdBefore` (ISO timestamp), `assigneeId`, `ruleId`. State values: OPEN, IN_PROGRESS, MITIGATED, RESOLVED, DUPLICATE, STATE_UNSPECIFIED. Severity: INFORMATIONAL, MEDIUM, HIGH, CRITICAL, CASE_SEVERITY_UNSPECIFIED. Pass null for other unused filters.\n\n**Sorting**: `orderByColumn` (`created_at` | `last_modified_at`), `orderByDirection` (`asc` | `desc`).\n\n**Multiple matches**: Present all with ID (prefer the sec-xxx short ID when displaying to the user) and distinguishing info; ask the user which one they want.\n\n**No match**: Tell the user no security case matched; suggest listing all security cases or trying a different description.\n'}}]);
